# Contributing to <%= it.projectName %>

Contribution guidelines covering development setup, branch conventions, PR process, code style, and review expectations.

## Development Setup

### Prerequisites

- <%= it.runtime %> >= [RUNTIME_VERSION]
- <%= it.pm.name %> >= [PACKAGE_MANAGER_VERSION]
- [ADDITIONAL_PREREQUISITES_OR_REMOVE]

### Local Environment

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone [REPO_URL]
cd <%= it.projectName %>

# Install dependencies
<%= it.installCommand %>

# Copy environment configuration
cp .env.example .env

# Start the development server
<%= it.devCommand %>

```

See `./docs/environment.md` for detailed environment variable documentation.

## Branch Conventions

| Pattern | Use For | Example |
|---------|---------|---------|
| `<%= it.defaultBranch %>` | Production-ready code | -- |
| `NNN-feature-name` | Feature branches | `001-user-auth` |

- `NNN`: Sequential feature number (001, 002, etc.)
- `feature-name`: 2-4 word kebab-case description
- Created by `/speckit-specify` or manually

Always branch from `<%= it.defaultBranch %>`.

## Commit Message Format

> **Convention**: This project uses [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/).
> If your team uses a different convention, update the commit type prefixes
> and format guidance below.

```
<prefix>(<scope>): <description>
```

| Prefix | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `feat` | New feature |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `docs` | Documentation changes |
| `style` | Formatting, no logic change |
| `refactor` | Code restructuring |
| `test` | Adding or updating tests |
| `chore` | Tooling, deps, config |
| `wip` | Checkpoint commit (auto-generated by `/checkpoint`) |

Keep the description under 72 characters. Use the body for additional context.

## Pull Request Process

1. Create a feature branch following the conventions above
2. Make focused, atomic commits with conventional prefixes
3. Ensure all tests pass locally: `<%= it.testCommand %>`
4. Run linting and fix any issues: `<%= it.lintCommand %>`
5. Update documentation if your change affects public APIs or behavior
6. Open a PR against `<%= it.defaultBranch %>` with a clear title and description

### PR Checklist

- [ ] Tests added or updated for the change
- [ ] Documentation updated (if applicable)
- [ ] No console logs, debug statements, or commented-out code
- [ ] Changelog updated under `[Unreleased]` in `./CHANGELOG.md`
- [ ] Self-reviewed the diff before requesting review

## Code Style

Follow the coding standards documented in `./docs/conventions.md`. Key points:

- Run `<%= it.lintCommand %>` before committing
- [FORMAT_ON_SAVE_OR_REMOVE] is configured for supported editors
- Naming conventions and file organization are enforced by linting rules

## Review Expectations

- PRs require **[REVIEW_COUNT]** approving review(s) before merge
- Reviewers should respond within **[REVIEW_SLA]** business days
- Address all review comments or explain why they are not applicable
- Use "Request Changes" for blocking issues, "Comment" for suggestions
- Squash-merge to `<%= it.defaultBranch %>`; maintain a clean commit history

---

Questions? Open a discussion or reach out to [MAINTAINER_CONTACT].
